From: iDeck local development <ideck-local@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Give QEMU generators the verified macOS build compiler

Class: build-fix

Evidence: experiments/linux-guest/evidence/qemu-host-compiler.json; Apple execution pending

The dedicated Linux Probe worker proves the separate build compiler with an
explicit macOS SDK and compiler default triple, then compiles, links and runs
a macOS-only probe. Pass those same validated tokens to QEMU's --host-cc.
Keep the iOS target compiler, flags, SDK and dependency search paths intact.

Offered-upstream: no, local experiment
---
diff --git a/scripts/build_ios.sh b/scripts/build_ios.sh
--- a/scripts/build_ios.sh
+++ b/scripts/build_ios.sh
@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@ stage_qemu() {
     ( cd "$dir/_husk_build" \
       && ../configure \
             --prefix="$PREFIX" \
             --cross-prefix="" \
+            --host-cc="${IDECK_QEMU_HOST_CC:?verified macOS build compiler is required}" \
             --target-list=aarch64-softmmu \
             --enable-shared-lib \
